;
; Demo Reel 3, from the Startup-Sequence.
;
; The demo assigns DemoReel3: and DemoReelData: itself -- both disks are
; merged into one drawer precisely so its own ToRAM can, when it finds
; Monument. So this only has to be in the right directory.
;
; DoWeHaveMem wants 1 MB; chip RAM here is 2 MB, so it should pass. ToRAM
; copies the tunes to RAM: and takes a while.
;
; Everything to DEBUG: so a machine that stops still says where.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel] --- what is on the volume"
List >DEBUG: DemoReel3/Slish DemoReel3/toram DemoReel3/Monument

Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel] --- ToRAM (assigns, 1 MB check, tunes to RAM:)"
CD DemoReel3
Execute toram
Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel] --- ToRAM returned"

Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel] --- assigns now"
Assign >DEBUG:

Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel] --- Slish"
Slish >DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel] --- Slish returned"
